    connections:
      "Ten ideas, one framework, organized around the SFB's real but partial consolidation: most sickness, disability, work-injury, and family benefits sit inside one Balk administered by Försäkringskassan, old-age pension sits inside the same Balk but under an entirely different agency, Pensionsmyndigheten, and unemployment insurance and municipal social assistance sit outside the SFB altogether, governed by their own separate statutes and institutions. Allmän pension, sjukpenning, aktivitetsersättning and sjukersättning, a-kassa, and arbetsskadeförsäkring each answer their own substantive entitlement question, with försörjningsstöd closing the lecture as the last-resort safety net beneath the entire contributory structure, exactly the role Grundsicherung plays beneath German social insurance or the RSA beneath the French system. Omprövning, återkrav, and bidragsbrottslagen then apply across nearly all of the contributory benefits, shared machinery layered over branch-specific substance, which is why they come last. Notice how often a distinctly Swedish mechanism does the same underlying job a different system hands to a different tool: the delningstal does with a notional-account division what other systems do with a flat percentage adjustment, and bidragsbrottslagen's gross-negligence standard does with a lower culpability bar what another system's intent requirement does with a higher one, each a genuinely Nordic answer to a problem every mature social-security system eventually has to solve. Learning this field well means tracking, concept by concept, which of Sweden's several separate institutions and statutes actually governs the question in front of you.",
